error[E0501]: cannot call `mut self` method `set_index` on `r`: it is not mutable
   --> tests/programs/interfaces/indexing/writes.la:13:5
   |
12 |     let r = Rows { rows: [[1]] };
   |         - declared here
13 |     r[0] = [2];
   |     ^
   |
   = help: make it mutable: `let mut r`

error[E0404]: `+=` can't change an element of `Rows` in place
   --> tests/programs/interfaces/indexing/writes.la:15:5
   |
15 |     s[0] += [3];
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: write `a[i] = a[i] + v`, which calls `index` and then `set_index`

error[E0502]: cannot assign to this expression
   --> tests/programs/interfaces/indexing/writes.la:16:5
   |
16 |     s[0][0] = 4;
   |     ^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: an element read by `index` is a copy: change it, then write it back with `let mut e = g[i]; e.x = v; g[i] = e;`

error[E0502]: cannot assign to this expression
   --> tests/programs/interfaces/indexing/writes.la:17:5
   |
17 |     s[0].push(5);
   |     ^^^^
   |
   = help: an element read by `index` is a copy: change it, then write it back with `let mut e = g[i]; e.x = v; g[i] = e;`

error[E0508]: cannot pass `s` to a `mut self` method called on `s`
   --> tests/programs/interfaces/indexing/writes.la:18:12
   |
18 |     s[0] = s.rows[0];
   |     -      ^
   |     |
   |     `s` is edited by this call
   |
   = help: copy it first: `let w = s;` and pass `w`

For more about E0501, E0404, E0502 and E0508, run `lughac explain <code>`.
